WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.140
Tyrion Lannister has some of the best lines
in Game of Thrones.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:09.150
He can be wise and funny and tragic and cruel,
sometimes all at once.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.709
It’s part of why he’s such a popular character.

00:00:11.709 --> 00:00:15.570
But Tyrion’s big mouth has often gotten
him into trouble.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:20.740
He’s pissed off a lot of people, and one
theory suggests that someday, someone will

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:26.439
shut Tyrion up for good – by cutting out
his tongue.

00:00:26.439 --> 00:00:29.519
Lots of people in Game of Thrones have their
tongues removed.

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:33.770
Ilyn Payne had his tongue cut out for talking
smack about the Mad King , and Marillion in

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:39.150
the show loses his for a singing a song . In
the books, Varys makes his little birds mute

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:43.890
, taking the tongues from these children so
they keep his secrets.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:48.570
Euron Greyjoy cuts out the tongues of the
crew of his ship , and others . And some Bolton

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:53.769
men lose their tongues . So sometimes it’s
about punishment, sometimes about keeping

00:00:53.769 --> 00:00:57.039
secrets, sometimes it’s just cruelty and
control.

00:00:57.039 --> 00:01:01.899
Lots of tongues come out for lots of reasons
– and some readers think Tyrion will be

00:01:01.899 --> 00:01:03.149
next.

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:06.860
Because Tyrion frequently gets threatened
with having his tongue cut out.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:12.610
Cersei and Joffrey and JonCon and Jorah and
Kurleket all threaten his tongue at some point.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:17.000
Both Bronn and Oberyn say that someone will
“cut it out one of these days” , and Tyrion

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.670
jokes he should do it himself, cause it causes
such trouble . So we’ve got all these direct

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:26.220
hints that someone will cut out Tyrion’s
tongue, and there are a few suspects who seem

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.860
especially likely.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:33.159
Cersei is weirdly obsessed with cutting out
tongues – she mentions the idea in about

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:38.340
half of her chapters . And Cersei deeply hates
Tyrion – she blames him for the death of

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:42.760
Joffrey, and is convinced that he’ll kill
her because of a prophecy . She’s especially

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:48.240
always hated the way he makes fun of her – his
mockery and criticism undermines her power

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:49.329
and pride.

00:01:49.329 --> 00:01:53.900
So if Cersei ever has Tyrion at her mercy
in the books, it’d totally fit for her to

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:57.030
finally silence her hated brother.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:01.180
Another possibility relates to the conspiracy
of Varys and Illyrio.

00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:05.829
In the books, there’s this kid called Young
Griff who Varys claims is Aegon Targaryen.

00:02:05.829 --> 00:02:11.290
Varys and Illyrio wanna put this Aegon on
the throne . But Tyrion seems to suspect that

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:17.610
the boy may not be a real Targaryen . Many
readers believe this Aegon is actually a Blackfyre

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.520
– go watch the Varys video.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.790
But the point is that Tyrion may learn a secret
that Varys doesn’t want getting out.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:30.000
And since Varys already has a habit of removing
tongues from people to keep his secrets – it’s

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.660
totally plausible that Varys or Illyrio might
cut out Tyrion’s tongue to protect their

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:38.300
conspiracy . A third possibility is Euron.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:43.161
Tyrion hasn’t met Euron in the books yet,
but Euron is becoming a big bad guy, and he

00:02:43.161 --> 00:02:48.330
cuts out lotsa tongues, so he might be a suspect
also.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:52.630
So it’s a strong possibility that Tyrion
may lose his tongue.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:56.530
And this could fit really well with the character
arcs of Tyrion’s family.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:03:01.290
At the start of the story, Tyrion’s brother
Jaime is defined by his ability to fight with

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:07.010
a sword . That is his source of power and
pride and identity – until in Book 3, his

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:13.500
hand is cut off, and Jaime has to redefine
who he is . “Who am I now?” he asks . Similarly,

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:18.780
Tyrion’s sister Cersei draws her power and
pride from her beauty and status , which is

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:24.280
symbolically stripped from her in this walk
of shame . So there’s this pattern of Lannisters

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:27.510
losing what gives them their pride and power.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:31.010
And the equivalent of Jaime’s hand is Tyrion’s
tongue.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:37.110
Cersei says that Tyrion wields “words as
skillfully as Jaime wields a sword” . If,

00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:41.780
like Jaime, Tyrion’s weapon is cut from
him, he’ll also have to redefine who he

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:42.810
is.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:48.830
Without a tongue, his passions for conversation,
politics, even food and sex, will be affected

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:52.580
– the meaning of his life will be at threat.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:57.480
This is a brutal thing to do to a character,
but author George Martin does it over and

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:02.770
over not only with Jaime and Cersei, but with
Bran, and Arya, and Theon.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:06.400
Bran loves to climb and ride, so George breaks
his back.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:10.510
Arya relies on her sight to survive, so George
blinds her.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:15.160
Theon uses sex to feel less insecure, so George
castrates him.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:20.230
When these characters lose what defines them,
they are forced to evolve – into a tree

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:23.220
god, a dark assassin, a hollow ghost.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:30.410
It’s “growth then decay, then transformation”
– and it makes for great storytelling.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:35.180
So Tyrion losing his tongue would fit not
only all the threats he’s received, and

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:40.590
the motivations of his enemies, and the pattern
in the Lannister family, but the author’s

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:46.220
overall strategy of breaking characters down
to see what they’re made of and what they

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.350
can become.

